      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for Packers And Movers Dhanbad To Solapur</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you hire <strong>packers movers in Dhanbad</strong> for a long‑haul shift to Solapur, the move is governed by a set of mandatory documents that protect both the client and the service provider. The first requirement is a GST‑compliant <em>e‑Way Bill</em>.</p>
<p>This electronic bill records the consignment’s value, GSTIN of the shipper, and the route, and it must be generated before the truck leaves Dhanbad. The e‑Way Bill not only ensures tax compliance but also enables real‑time tracking by customs and state authorities.</p>

<p>Alongside the e‑Way Bill, the transporter must issue an <strong>IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR) or Bilty</strong>. This receipt serves as the legal proof of carriage, detailing the weight, dimensions, and declared value of every item – from a bulky sofa to a delicate refrigerator.</p>
<p>The LR is signed by the consignor, the driver, and the moving company, creating a clear chain of custody that can be referenced in case of disputes.</p>

<p>To safeguard the financial risk of loss or damage, reputable firms provide a <strong>100 % declared‑value IRDAI marine transit insurance</strong>. This policy, mandated by the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI), covers accidental collisions, fire, theft, and even unforeseen delays that could jeopardise time‑sensitive goods.</p>
<p>The insurance premium is calculated on the total declared value, ensuring you are fully compensated if any mishap occurs during the Dhanbad‑to‑Solapur leg.</p>

